+# Design
+
+## Approach
+
+Trace product deletion through the core entity relationships and remove hard dependencies from cart and order read paths. Cart persistence can continue to identify a line by product id, but cart hydration/recalculation must tolerate a missing product and discard that line before exposing or checking out the cart. Product resolution used by add-to-cart and v2 lookup must distinguish a missing/deleted record and surface the existing not-found API response.
+
+Order lines need to be historical snapshots rather than requiring a live product join. Populate the order-line snapshot fields at order creation, make the entity/read mappers use those fields when the product association is absent, and ensure deletion mappings do not cascade into order lines or their totals. Verify all four order read routes and status mutation with integration tests, plus cart update/multi-update and checkout paths.
+
+## Affected Areas
+
+- Core product, shopping-cart, order, and persistence mappings/services.
+- Shop cart, product, checkout, and order facades/controllers and DTO conversion.
+- Existing integration-test support and API tests.
+
+## Compatibility and Data
+
+Use nullable/optional product associations for legacy and newly deleted rows while retaining existing serialized order values. Do not recalculate persisted order totals from current catalog data. Existing non-deleted product behavior and unrelated product rows must remain unchanged.
+
+## Verification
+
+Run focused module tests first, then the repository Maven test/build command available in the checkout. Add regression tests at the service/API boundary so a deleted product is created, used in a cart/order, deleted, and then exercised through each required endpoint.
