+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Product deletion currently removes data that carts and orders still need to render and process. This makes historical orders unreadable and can prevent carts from being opened or checked out, so deletion of a discontinued product must be isolated from those historical and in-progress records.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Make persisted cart lines resilient to a deleted product: omit unavailable lines when carts are read or recalculated, recompute quantities and totals from remaining lines, and permit subsequent cart updates and checkout.
+- Reject adding a deleted product with HTTP 404 while preserving normal behavior for all other products.
+- Preserve order-line snapshots (SKU, name, quantity, price, subtotal) independently of the product row so all merchant and customer order endpoints, totals, and status updates continue to work after deletion.
+- Return HTTP 404 from the v2 public product lookup for a deleted SKU without changing other product lookups.
+- Add regression coverage for deletion, cart recovery, checkout, order reads/status updates, and unrelated-product isolation.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `deleted-product-safety`: Carts and order history remain usable and accurate after a product is deleted, while new access to the deleted product is rejected.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- None.
+
+## Impact
+
+The product deletion flow, shopping-cart services/facades and API controllers, checkout/order creation and read mapping, v2 product lookup, persistence mappings, and integration/unit tests are affected. Existing order totals and historical line values must remain unchanged.
